  * GPU VA window 8-16 GB: L1[8..15] -> L2 (512 x 2 MB) -> L3 (512 x 4 KB).
  * L2/L3 tables are 4 KB, carved from 16 KB pages; L3 tables are allocated
  * on first use of a 2 MB chunk and kept. Mappings are page (16 KB)
- * granular, first fit from a rover, each followed by one unmapped guard
- * page (a GPU overrun faults instead of hitting the next buffer): Mesa
- * makes thousands of small buffers, whole 2 MB chunks ran out at 4096.
- * g_owner[page] is the mapping index (0 free, VM_GUARD guard).
+ * granular, first fit from a rover, each followed by VM_PAD padding pages
+ * that all map one shared scratch page: texture/vertex fetch reads past
+ * buffer ends, and a fault there hung the A530 even with faults
+ * terminated (0154a/c, 0155a), so overruns land in scratch instead.
+ * Mesa makes thousands of small buffers, whole 2 MB chunks ran out at 4096.
+ * g_owner[page] is the mapping index (0 free, VM_GUARD padding).
  */
 #define GVA_BASE        0x200000000ull
 #define GVA_CHUNKS      4096u                   /* 8 GB / 2 MB */
 #define GVA_PAGES       ((uint32_t)((8ull << 30) / PAGE_SIZE))
 #define VM_MAPS         16384u                  /* index 0 unused */
 #define VM_GUARD        0xffffu
+#define VM_PAD          8u                      /* 128 KB */
 #define PTE_ATTRS       ((1u << 6) | (2u << 8) | (1u << 10))    /* AP[1], SH outer, AF; AttrIndx 0 */
 
